{title: Heavenly Places (Nowhere else)}
{artist: Daniel Sullivan}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 66}

Verse 1
I want to stay here, here in your presence
In heavenly places, to abide in the vine

Verse 2
I want to breathe in, your heavenly fragrance
To sit at your table, to drink the new wine

Chorus
For there is nowhere else I'd rather be
Than in your anointing Lord, where I am made free
Open my eyes Jesus to the things I don't see
Oh my savoir I love you

Verse 3
I want to clearly hear, your righteous thunder
To be being filled, with your Holy fire

Verse 4
Make me to know and walk, in the way of your judgments
For to keep your commandments, is my soul's desire

Chorus
For there is nowhere else I'd rather be
Than in your anointing Lord, where I am made free
Open my eyes Jesus to the things I don't see
Oh my savoir I love you

Chorus
For there is nowhere else I'd rather be
Than in your anointing Lord, where I am made free
Open my eyes Jesus to the things I don't see
Oh my savoir I love you
